data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Core mechanism:** Cas9 paired with a synthetic guide RNA cuts DNA at a chosen site. The cell's repair then either disrupts the gene or, with a supplied template, inserts new DNA [6][3].\n- **Dominant uses:** Knocking out genes is the most common application. Repair templates can also replace disease-causing mutations with healthy sequences [2].\n- **Expanding therapeutic claims:** Coverage points to disease treatment [4] and HIV elimination in cell culture [5]. These are early, and the sources are headlines or culture-level results, not clinical outcomes."}

